只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Build and reuse WebMCP tools in a macOS desktop workspace for DeepSeek Harness.","id":"gh:1336615760","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"DeepDeck","slug":"jo32/DeepDeck","topics":["ai-agent","browser-automation","cordis","deepdeck","deepseek","deepseek-harness","desktop-app","dsh-plugin","electron","macos","webmcp"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Build and reuse WebMCP tools in a macOS desktop workspace for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"DeepDeck"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Build and reuse WebMCP tools in a macOS desktop workspace for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Download for Mac · Apple Silicon / Intel ·\nWebsite ·\nTry it ·\nBrowser guide"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Describe a website task. DeepDeck's Agent can use the site's existing WebMCP tools, or explore its i"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"nterface and build tools you can inspect and reuse later. Source and saved versions stay available f"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"or review, disabling, and rollback."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"| Build tools for a website | Reuse them for a task |"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| In this X example, Builder creates 23 tools for reading pages, searching, and editing drafts. | Sw"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"itch to Use and ask for a Hello world draft. The example fills the draft without publishing it. |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Initial exploration and verification take time and tokens. Reuse benefits depend on the task and too"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"l design; site changes can require revalidation. Measured savings are not yet established."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Try it"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"1. Download the latest release, choose the DMG for your Mac, and open DeepDeck. Set up a model in Se"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ttings if you have not already configured Harness.\n2. Open **Browser**, visit a site, and open **Sit"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"e Agent → WebMCP** to inspect any tools the website provides.\n3. If a needed tool is missing, switch"},{"id":"p10s4","text":" to **Builder** and describe what it should do. Review the generated tools and validation results, t"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"hen return to **Use** and ask for the task."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"DeepDeck is a macOS desktop application. Install it from Releases; a generic `dsh plugin add` comman"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"d does not install the desktop app or its native browser bridge. For development from source, see Fi"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ot install the desktop app or its native browser bridge. For development from source, see First run."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Browser + WebMCP"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**Download the latest DeepDeck release** for Apple Silicon and Intel Macs."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**Let the Agent use a website, then keep what it learns as WebMCP tools.** You describe the goal. Th"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"e Agent explores the real site, tries its workflows, checks the results, and saves the working opera"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"tions as reusable tools. Building WebMCP is like preserving the Agent's experience of using the webs"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"ite, so future tasks can reuse it without a person writing step-by-step instructions."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"That experience lives in inspectable, executable tools: how to search, read results, or edit and ver"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ify a draft. DeepDeck Browser supports both **reusing WebMCP tools that already exist** and **quickl"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"y building tools for websites that do not have them**, making existing products easier for agents to"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"tools for websites that do not have them**, making existing products easier for agents to work with."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"#### What is WebMCP?"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"WebMCP is a proposed web API that lets websites expose JavaScript functions or HTML forms as tools w"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ith natural-language descriptions and structured input schemas. An agent can discover what a website"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" does, supply the right arguments, and call its tools within the current page, sharing the user's br"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"owser context and visible interface. It complements backend MCP integrations."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"#### WebMCP vs. ordinary computer use"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Computer use operates a website through its interface: observe, locate controls, click or type, then"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" observe again. WebMCP exposes named capabilities with descriptions and input schemas, so the model "},{"id":"p20s3","text":"can call a tool and read its result. See the WebMCP project's motivation and goals."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| | Ordinary computer use | WebMCP |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Understanding | Infer functionality and state from screenshots or page structure. | Discover expli"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"cit tool names, descriptions, and parameters. |\n| Execution | Locate and operate controls across mul"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"tiple observation/action steps. | Supply arguments to a tool; it performs the corresponding operatio"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"ns and returns a result. |\n| Reuse | Usually repeat the UI steps; reuse requires separately saving a"},{"id":"p22s5","text":" script or workflow. | DeepDeck saves verified operations as tools that later tasks can reuse. |\n| T"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"ime and tokens | Repeated page reads and model decisions add overhead. | For tasks covered by tools,"},{"id":"p22s7","text":" fewer observation and interaction rounds can save time and tokens. |\n| Best suited to | Exploring s"},{"id":"p22s8","text":"ites and handling interactions without existing tools. | Calling existing tools and reusing recurrin"},{"id":"p22s9","text":"g website workflows. |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"For example, **searching for a keyword and reading the results** with computer use typically means f"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"inding the search field, typing, submitting, reading the new page, and extracting results. With WebM"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"CP, the Agent calls a search tool with the keyword and reads the result, using a separate results-re"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ading tool if needed."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"**DeepDeck combines both approaches.** The Agent explores and verifies a website through browser int"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"eraction, then saves working operations as WebMCP tools. Later tasks can reuse that experience, with"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" browser interaction available for anything the tools do not cover. Initial tool building takes expl"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"oration and verification; savings depend on the website, tool design, and task, and site changes may"},{"id":"p24s5","text":" require tool updates."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"#### 1. Reuse existing WebMCP"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Open a website, select **Site Agent → WebMCP**, and inspect the tools discovered under **Website**. "},{"id":"p26s2","text":"In **Use** mode, describe your task and the Agent can call the available tools. The screenshot below"},{"id":"p26s3","text":" shows DeepDeck discovering `search_openai` on openai.com."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"DeepDeck is a native-feeling desktop client built on DeepSeek Harness. The upstream project is pinne"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"d to **0.2.1-rc.2** (`687f282e86`) as a shallow Git submodule at `vendor/deepseek-harness`. Plugin d"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"evelopment dependencies link to this same checkout, including the Cordis and Schemastery libraries t"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"hat have not yet been published at the RC’s required versions; this repository owns the desktop life"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"cycle, plugin-composed interface, branding, packaging, and automatic-update layer. dsh-codex-connect"},{"id":"p28s6","text":" remains a separate pinned checkout and is preloaded as an ordinary Cordis bundle."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"DeepDeck reuses the official `web` profile and its complete plugin-composed UI. The desktop host sta"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"rts the Harness process on an OS-assigned loopback port, waits for it to become ready, then opens th"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"e local UI in the application window. Closing the app shuts the Harness process down cleanly."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Plugins can be discovered and installed from the dshfind-backed market in **Settings → Apps**. DeepD"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"eck treats dshfind as a discovery catalog: it validates the selected GitHub repository and DSH bundl"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"e, previews the build plan, installs dependencies with lifecycle scripts disabled, and requires conf"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"irmation before running the plugin's own build script. Trusted local plugin source can also be compi"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"led from **Settings → Plugins → Bun Builder**."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
